AU  - Lopuran, Felix; Gikunda, Patrick; Moso, Juliet
TI  - Hybrid Deep Learning Model for Spermatozoa Movement Analysis and Male Infertility Diagnosis Using U-Net, Yolov8, and Deepsort
PY  - 2025
AB  - Infertility is a major global health issue, impacting 17.5 % of adults. Male infertility significantly contributes to this, emphasizing the need for improved diagnostic methods. This paper presents a hybrid deep learning approach for analysing spermatozoa movement and diagnosing male infertility by integrating UNet for segmentation, YOLOv8 for detection, and DeepSORT for tracking. Using the VISEM Tracking dataset, the proposed model pipeline isolates, labels, and tracks individual sperm cells, achieving high accuracy and efficiency in identifying motility patterns essential for male infertility diagnosis. The pipeline demonstrated a segmentation accuracy of 98.21 % with U-Net, Mean average precision of 98.43 % using YOLOv8, and robust tracking results with a MOTA (Multi Object Tracking Accuracy) of 90.41 % through DeepSORT. This integrated approach provides reliable, data-driven insights into sperm health, enhancing clinical diagnostics for male infertility.
