AU  - Jiao, Wentan; Li, Yang; Lv, Longtao
TI  - Study on Sperm Morphology Analysis Using Deep Learning
PY  - 2024
AB  - Sperm morphology analysis is important in diagnosing male infertility problems. Due to the low pixel count of existing public sperm morphology datasets, a sperm morphology dataset based on the improved Papanicolaou stain was produced. In this work, we propose a semantic segmentation network for sperm morphology that contains encoding, decoding, and spatial attention modules. Firstly, a pre-trained model is introduced in the encoder part, then a spatial attention module is added in the jump connection part, and finally an asymmetric hybrid dilated convolution is proposed in the decoder part to obtain contextual information at different scales and orientations. The experimental results show that compared with similar methods, this method has better performance in mean intersection over union, mean accuracy, mean pixel accuracy and mean F1-score in a sperm dataset containing 13 different morphologies. Among the 4 evaluation indicators, the average improvements were 11.18%, 11.78%, 6.00% and 9.38% respectively, with better segmentation accuracy and generalization ability.
