AU  - C, Jansi Sophia Mary.; V, Elamathi.; A, Thamizharuvi.; J, Swathi.; M, Gomathi.
TI  - RCNN-based Embryo In Vitro Fertilization (IVF) Concept
PY  - 2025
AB  - In vitro fertilization (IVF) axes the capacity to select viable embryos for transfer and pregnancy. Traditional methods depend on comparisons of morphological assessments done manually by a human embryologist, which are mutable, subjective, and observer-dependent. In response, an automatic deep learning system to improve the accuracy of the embryo selection is suggested. It is used for preprocessing like noise removal, contrast enhancement, and region scaling to enhance image quality and emphasize relevant features. Embryos detection and segmentation were done using a Region-based Convolutional Neural Network (RCNN) to select Regions of Interest (ROI) and classify them according to their developmental stage and quality. The RCNN model is trained over annotated embryo images scored by experts, which can extract and learn both morphological features of clinical importance. This method substantially minimizes human bias, quickens the assessment process, and enhances the consistency of embryo grading. The system has extracted correct information with a precision of 96% and recall of 96%, giving the F1-score 94% significant result. This AI-enabled workflow is a scalable solution for embryology labs, enabling better IVF results, real-time mirroring, and decision support in reproductive medicine.
