AU  - Zhu, Jianbo; Jiang, Tao; Grzegorzek, Marcin; Li, Chen
TI  - FFE-FRCN: A Frequency Feature Enhanced Few-Shot Learning Approach for Object Detection in Microscopic Images
PY  - 2025
AB  - As the demand for Microscopic Image Analysis (MIA) increases, object detection in deep learning has gradually become a popular research area. Considering the high cost of microscopic image acquisition and dataset preparation, training data is often insufficient and imbalanced. Few-shot Object Detection (FSOD) offers a new approach. However, current FSOD methods have not fully utilized color and texture characteristics when processing microscopic images, which still have potential performance that has not been explored. Therefore, we propose Frequency-domain Feature Enhanced Faster-RCNN (FFEFRCN), which includes a frequency-enhanced feature pyramid network, gradient decoupling layers, and a channel attention calibration block. We conducted benchmark experiments on the Environmental Microorganism Image Dataset Seventh Version (EMDS-7) and extended experiments on the Sperm Videos and Images Analysis (SVIA). Experimental results show that our model achieved superior performance. On EMDS-7, we achieved an mAP50 and nAP50 of 56.06 % and 41.00 % at 1-shot, and 73.39 % and 69.20 % respectively at 8 -shots. On SVIA, we achieved an AP50 of 96.49 % for sperm and 70.21 % for impurity.
