AU  - Tiab, Idir; Belaid, Ahror; Yahiaoui, Saïd; Belazzougui, Djamal; Hafsi, Nabil; Iguer-Ouada, Mokrane
TI  - Deep Characterization For Sperm Analysis: Leveraging A Novel Dataset To Enhance Motility Assessments
PY  - 2024
AB  - Microscopic imaging techniques have been developed to assess sperm quality by analysing morphology, motility and other parameters. The study presented in this paper introduces an automatic computer-assisted analysis (CASA) system driven by deep learning. It covers species classification, sperm detection and tracking, and sample quality analysis. Our first contribution is the introduction of a new curated and well-labeled dataset specifically designed for sperm analysis, addressing the crucial need for diverse data in this field. To the best of to our knowledge, there exists no extensive dataset encompassing a wide variety and volume of sperm species. The proposed dataset will thus serve as a substantial contribution in this domain. The second contribution consists in the training and testing of state-of-the art deep-learning models (MobileNet, YOLOv5s, and DeepSort) on our proposed data sets as well as on of the widely used VISEM dataset [1]. Extensive assessment for classification, detection, and tracking has yielded promising results: classification accuracy of 99.2%, detection results ranging from 96% to 99.5% mAP@50, and a tracking MOTP of 99%. Rigorous testing across various sperm species provides vital parameters for sperm motility assessment.
