AU  - Kirtika, K; Gajalakshmi, P; Priya, S Catherine; Palanivel, G
TI  - Comparative Analysis of Optimizers for YOLOv11 based Object Detection
PY  - 2026
AB  - Optimizers play an important role in the accuracy and efficiency of convolutional neural networks by controlling the updates of convolutional neural networks parameters in the training process. The literature does not have a comprehensive discussion of adaptive optimizers such as Adam, AdamW and AdaBelief on the FLIR ADAS V2 thermal imaging dataset in the context of the YOLOv11 architecture, thus this paper is a novel comparison of these adaptive optimizers. The original contributions encompass: (1) the performance evaluation of AdaBelief as an empirical experiment (with mAP@50, mAP@50-95, and training time as key metrics); (2) the discovery of the optimal hyperparameters, in particular, the fact that a momentum of 0.937 is an effective one to use; and (3), the actionable conclusions about the forging of optimal hyperparameters in place of object detecting systems which use infrared cameras. Findings demonstrate that AdaBelief attains better mAP@50 (0.696) at the lowest training cost (6.999 hrs), which is an important point of reference when operating real-time vision in the defense and autonomous devices.
